# Vercel Speed Insights Implementation

## Summary
Successfully installed and configured Vercel Speed Insights for the Rovauto project following the latest official documentation from Vercel.

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- Installed `@vercel/speed-insights@^2.0.0` using npm
- Updated `package.json` with the new dependency
- Updated `package-lock.json` with dependency lock information

### 2. Configuration
**Modified: `client/src/App.jsx`**
- Added import statement: `import { SpeedInsights } from "@vercel/speed-insights/react";`
- Added `<SpeedInsights />` component in the App root component, right next to the existing `<Analytics />` component
- This placement ensures Speed Insights is loaded across all pages of the application

## Implementation Details

Following the official Vercel Speed Insights documentation, I used the React-specific integration approach:
- For React applications, the `<SpeedInsights />` component should be imported from `@vercel/speed-insights/react`
- The component is placed at the root level of the application to track performance across all routes
- The implementation follows the same pattern as the existing Vercel Analytics integration

## Files Modified
1. `client/package.json` - Added @vercel/speed-insights dependency
2. `client/package-lock.json` - Updated with new dependency locks
3. `client/src/App.jsx` - Added SpeedInsights import and component

## Testing & Verification
✅ Build completed successfully with no errors
✅ All dependencies installed correctly
✅ Speed Insights component integrated following React best practices
✅ Implementation matches existing code patterns (similar to Analytics integration)

## Next Steps
To complete the setup:
1. Deploy the application to Vercel
2. Enable Speed Insights in the Vercel dashboard for this project
3. After a few days of visitor traffic, metrics will become available in the Vercel dashboard

## Notes
- The project is built with Vite + React
- Speed Insights is now configured to work alongside the existing Vercel Analytics integration
- No breaking changes were introduced
- The integration is framework-optimized for React applications
